### create_link_anchors (bundle link.rs:20-63)
```rust
pub fn create_link_anchors(
    items: &mut [Item],
    targets: &FxHashMap<&VirtualPath, FxHashSet<Location>>,
) -> FxHashMap<Location, EcoString> {
    let empty = FxHashSet::default();
    let mut anchors: FxHashMap<Location, EcoString> = items
        .par_iter_mut()
        .flat_map_iter(|item| {
            let Item::Document(path, doc, _) = item else {
                return Either::Right([].iter().cloned());
            };
            let targets = targets.get(path).unwrap_or(&empty);
            match doc {
                BundleDocument::Html(doc) => Either::Left(
                    typst_html::create_link_anchors(
                        doc.as_mut(),
                        &targets.iter().copied().collect(),
                    )
                    .into_iter(),
                ),
                BundleDocument::Paged(doc, options) => {
                    options.anchors = create_paged_link_anchors(doc, targets);
                    Either::Right(options.anchors.iter().cloned())
                }
            }
        })
        .collect();

    // Create empty anchors for assets and documents so that we can also link
    // directly at them.
    for item in items {
        let loc = match item {
            Item::Tag(_) => continue,
            Item::Asset(.., loc) => loc,
            Item::Document(.., loc) => loc,
        };
        anchors.insert(*loc, EcoString::new());
    }

    anchors
}
```

Key points:
- Takes `&mut [Item]` because it mutates documents in place (HTML DOM injection; paged writes into `options.anchors`).
- Parallelized with rayon `par_iter_mut`.
- For each Document item, looks up its target set from the map (or empty), then dispatches:
  - HTML: `typst_html::create_link_anchors(doc, targets)` mutates DOM in place, returns `FxHashMap<Location, EcoString>` (loc→id). Returns via `Either::Left`.
  - Paged: `create_paged_link_anchors(doc, targets)` returns `Vec<(Location, EcoString)>`, stored into `options.anchors` (the PagedExtras sidecar). Returns the (loc, anchor) pairs via `Either::Right`.
- `flat_map_iter` + `collect` flattens all `(Location, EcoString)` pairs into one global map. Note HTML returns `(loc, id)` pairs directly (HashMap entries), paged returns `Vec<(loc, anchor)>` cloned.
- The return type is `FxHashMap<Location, EcoString>` — the global anchor map (loc → anchor string), local to each file.
- Note: it skips `Item::Tag` and `Item::Asset` in the first loop (the `else` branch returns empty). Assets don't have link targets inside them.
- The empty anchors loop: for every Tag/Asset/Document item, insert its own location → empty string `EcoString::new()`. This makes documents and assets themselves linkable (a link to the document's own location resolves to an empty anchor = "link to the whole document"). Tags too get empty anchors.

