### AnchorGenerator (library link.rs:515-555) + identify + can_use_label_as_id + disambiguate
```rust
pub fn identify(&mut self, label: Option<Label>) -> EcoString {
    if let Some(label) = label {
        let resolved = label.resolve();
        let text = resolved.as_str();
        if can_use_label_as_id(text) {
            if self.introspector.label_count(label) == 1 {
                return text.into();
            }
            let counter = self.label_counter.entry(label).or_insert(0);
            *counter += 1;
            return disambiguate(self.introspector, text, counter);
        }
    }
    self.loc_counter += 1;
    disambiguate(self.introspector, "loc", &mut self.loc_counter)
}
```
- If element has a label that's a valid CSS id + URL fragment (`can_use_label_as_id`): reuse it. If unique (`label_count == 1`), use as-is. If duplicate, append `-N`.
- Else generate `loc-N`.
- `disambiguate` loops to avoid colliding with an existing label turned into `<label>`.

### Empty anchors + consumption (LateLinkResolver, library link.rs:652-694, ResolvedLink 698-715, into_relative_uri 724-748)
```rust
pub fn resolve(&self, location: Location) -> Option<ResolvedLink> {
    let from = self.base;
    let to = self.introspector.path(location);
    let anchor = self.introspector.anchor(location)?.clone();
    Some(match (from, to) {
        (None, None) => ResolvedLink::Local { anchor },
        (Some(from), Some(to)) => {
            if from == to {
                ResolvedLink::Local { anchor }
            } else {
                ResolvedLink::Cross { from: from.clone(), to: to.clone(), anchor }
            }
        }
        (Some(_), None) => return None,
        (None, Some(_)) => return None,
    })
}
```
- `anchor` comes from `introspector.anchor(location)` which reads the `anchors` map set by `set_anchors`. This is the connection: create_link_anchors → set_anchors → anchor() → LateLinkResolver::resolve.
- For a document/asset link (empty anchor), `anchor` = "" → `ResolvedLink::Local { anchor: "" }` or `Cross { ..., anchor: "" }`.
- `into_relative_uri`: Local empty → `#`; Cross empty → just the relative path (no trailing #). Non-empty → `path#anchor`.

So the empty anchor for documents/assets is what makes "link to the whole document" work, producing a clean relative path without a fragment.

